    "id": "dynamo-disagg",
    "caption": "Dynamo's router picks a prefill worker by cached prefix and load; the prefill worker computes the KV cache and hands it to a decode worker over NIXL, which streams the tokens.",
    "alt": "A client calls the Dynamo frontend's OpenAI-compatible API. The router consults a global index of which KV blocks each worker holds and picks a prefill worker. The prefill worker computes the prompt's KV cache and transfers it with NIXL over NVLink or RDMA to a decode worker in a separate pool, which streams tokens back to the client. The KV Block Manager can offload cache blocks to CPU memory, SSD or remote storage. The Planner watches TTFT and ITL and resizes the prefill and decode pools.",
